### IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client. Sandbox API key: sandbox-key
@base = http://localhost:8085
@apiKey = sandbox-key

### 1. New card (use a card number from the N-Genius sandbox test cards)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/payments
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: SO-1001-attempt-1
X-Correlation-Id: demo-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "merchantOrderId": "SO-1001",
  "cardType": "CARD",
  "returnUrl": "http://localhost:3000/checkout/done?order=SO-1001",
  "card": { "pan": "<sandbox-test-card>", "expiry": "2030-12", "cvv": "123", "cardholderName": "Jane Doe" },
  "amount": { "value": 250.00, "currency": "AED" },
  "billingInfo": { "firstName": "Jane", "lastName": "Doe", "email": "jane@example.com",
                   "address": "Sheikh Zayed Road 1", "city": "Dubai", "countryCode": "AE" },
  "deviceInfo": { "ip": "203.0.113.10", "userAgent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Macintosh; Intel Mac OS X 10_15_7)",
                  "acceptHeader": "text/html,application/xhtml+xml", "language": "en", "timeZoneOffset": "-240",
                  "screenWidth": "1440", "screenHeight": "900", "colorDepth": "24",
                  "javascriptEnabled": true, "javaEnabled": false, "challengeWindowSize": "05" }
}

### 2. Card on file (saved N-Genius token; CVV still required)
POST {{base}}/api/v1/payments
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: SO-1002-attempt-1
X-Correlation-Id: demo-2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "merchantOrderId": "SO-1002",
  "cardType": "CARD_ON_FILE",
  "card": { "token": "<saved-ni-card-token>", "expiry": "2030-12", "cvv": "123", "cardholderName": "Jane Doe" },
  "amount": { "value": 99.00, "currency": "AED" },
  "billingInfo": { "firstName": "Jane", "lastName": "Doe", "email": "jane@example.com" },
  "deviceInfo": { "ip": "203.0.113.10", "userAgent": "Mozilla/5.0", "acceptHeader": "text/html", "language": "en" }
}

### 3. Validation error example: CARD_ON_FILE with a pan instead of a token -> 400
POST {{base}}/api/v1/payments
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Idempotency-Key: SO-1003-attempt-1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "merchantOrderId": "SO-1003",
  "cardType": "CARD_ON_FILE",
  "card": { "pan": "4111111111111111", "expiry": "2030-12", "cvv": "123", "cardholderName": "Jane Doe" },
  "amount": { "value": 10.00, "currency": "AED" },
  "billingInfo": { "firstName": "Jane", "lastName": "Doe", "email": "jane@example.com" },
  "deviceInfo": { "ip": "203.0.113.10", "userAgent": "Mozilla/5.0", "acceptHeader": "text/html", "language": "en" }
}

### 4. Current status (paste a paymentId from a response above)
GET {{base}}/api/v1/payments/<paymentId>
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 5. 3DS challenge page (HTML) for a CHALLENGE_REQUIRED payment, e.g. to show in a WebView
GET {{base}}/api/v1/threeds/<paymentId>/challenge
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}

### 6. Send the cres the ACS posted to your returnUrl
POST {{base}}/api/v1/threeds/<paymentId>/challenge-response
X-Api-Key: {{apiKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cres": "<base64-cres-from-the-acs>" }

### 7. 3DS challenge result, as the card issuer's ACS makes the shopper's browser post it (no API key).
### Only for payments without returnUrl.
### Normally sent by the browser after the challenge; here only to see the redirect / result page.
POST {{base}}/api/v1/threeds/<paymentId>/notification
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

cres=<base64-cres-from-the-acs>
